WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.180
Augustine of Hippo, a
North African bishop,

2
00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.530
remembered a prayer from his youth.

3
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.040
Give me chastity and
continency, only not yet.

4
00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:11.870
He wanted to do right.

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.720
Part of him did not.

6
00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:16.880
He felt two wills struggling inside him.

7
00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:20.870
Why do people do wrong, even
when they want to do right?

8
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.330
In this mission, you'll follow Augustine's
reading of the first humans in Eden,

9
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.710
before and after the Fall.

10
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.830
Then you'll weigh up whether his
view of human nature is pessimistic,

11
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.120
realistic or hopeful.

12
00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:39.390
Your mission: find out how Augustine
explains the struggle inside the human will.
